# UST.G3DP H02 Four-Prime Reconstruction Holdout Theorem v1

## Status

`CLOSED_EXACT_FOUR_PRIME_RECONSTRUCTION_WITH_INDEPENDENT_FIFTH_PRIME_HOLDOUT`

G3DP reconstructs every normalized H02 kernel coefficient from the first four
split primes within the rational uniqueness range. It then tests that candidate
against the complete G3DO residue at the previously unused prime 68,213.

The construction modulus is

```text
M4 = 1,055,707,942,588,321,339
```

and the uniqueness bound is 726,535,595. The fifth prime is not consulted
until every four-prime candidate is fixed.

## Exact outcome

The packet records:

```text
four-prime candidates
fifth-prime holdout passes
rejected four-prime aliases
retained prior passes
lost prior passes
newly stable coefficients beyond the three-prime range
```

for all 46,032,168 coefficients and separately for each of the six power-basis
degrees. Canonical pass and candidate masks are persisted.

## Boundary

Five-prime agreement remains finite evidence. G3DP does not claim an exact
`Q(gamma)` relation, rank equality in characteristic zero, source contraction,
path integration, integral marking, readout or `beta_C`.

The five-prime modulus exceeds signed 64-bit range, so G3DP deliberately does
not construct a five-prime candidate. The next executor must use unsigned
128-bit or multiprecision arithmetic and reserve the sixth split prime for a
new holdout.

## Reproduction

```powershell
python build_ust_g3dp_h02_four_prime_reconstruction_holdout.py
```

